WEBVTT

00:11.470 --> 00:13.600
(The Night Before Entering Tenebre)

00:14.730 --> 00:15.550
Yuke.

00:16.710 --> 00:18.740
There's one thing I want to decide on now.

00:19.210 --> 00:20.489
Uncle Saga?

00:20.490 --> 00:21.860
Our order of entry.

00:23.420 --> 00:25.589
Once we get to the Abyss Gate,

00:25.590 --> 00:28.070
someone is going to have to close it.

00:28.620 --> 00:31.120
But the one who does...

00:31.960 --> 00:34.360
...might never be able to come back.

00:35.510 --> 00:40.250
So I'll go first, and you'll
go second. All right?

00:41.370 --> 00:42.360
Okay.

00:43.370 --> 00:45.170
And the third will be...

00:48.030 --> 00:49.030
me.

00:57.160 --> 01:04.130
(I Left My A-Rank Party to Help My Former
Students Reach the Dungeon Depths)

02:18.980 --> 02:24.990
(Episode 24:
Beyond the Dream)

02:33.840 --> 02:34.960
We're almost there.

02:35.310 --> 02:37.200
A huge... gate?

02:37.560 --> 02:39.839
This is the Abyss Gate?

02:39.840 --> 02:41.460
No, it's not.

02:41.840 --> 02:43.210
This is the seal.

02:43.670 --> 02:46.309
Benwood, myself, and the
others in our party sealed it

02:46.310 --> 02:48.640
to keep the Abyss Gate here.

02:49.720 --> 02:53.079
The bridge between worlds,
the door to other worlds...

02:53.080 --> 02:55.219
None of those are wrong,

02:55.220 --> 02:59.110
but there's a more accurate description,
and I think you know what it is.

03:00.190 --> 03:01.080
A culling.

03:01.810 --> 03:06.740
Yes. This world has been exposed
to a culling for a long time now.

03:07.100 --> 03:10.240
Since the day you and the rest
of the advance party came here?

03:10.500 --> 03:12.499
Maybe even before that.

03:12.500 --> 03:15.099
Dungeons everywhere went berserk,

03:15.100 --> 03:17.250
and there were frequent Stampedes.

03:23.510 --> 03:28.090
Your hometown was the first place in this
world to be swallowed up by Tenebre.

03:28.950 --> 03:30.249
I know.

03:30.250 --> 03:33.350
I was very young, and you saved me.

03:35.740 --> 03:38.170
I need to apologize to you...

03:38.730 --> 03:41.110
For luring you onto the
path of the adventurer,

03:41.550 --> 03:43.880
and for bringing you here now.

03:44.950 --> 03:47.389
Help me, Yuke.

03:47.390 --> 03:48.860
Only you,

03:49.480 --> 03:53.870
someone who's been touched by the
other side, can beat that thing.

03:54.550 --> 03:56.120
Feel free to hate me...

03:56.510 --> 03:58.870
but you're the only one who can do this.

04:06.690 --> 04:10.760
Everyone, look. This is what has
become of the Abyss Gate.

04:11.240 --> 04:13.680
That's it? Are you serious?

04:14.620 --> 04:19.439
I get it. It came through
the door to get here.

04:19.440 --> 04:22.410
So that itself is the culling.

04:25.330 --> 04:27.359
Yes, the culling.

04:27.360 --> 04:30.569
The other world that came to our
own through Achromatic Darkness

04:30.570 --> 04:32.820
connects all worlds together.

04:33.700 --> 04:35.700
That thing is the aggregate
of that concept.

04:39.330 --> 04:41.839
So whatever that thing is, it's an enemy.

04:41.840 --> 04:43.840
Sure doesn't look friendly to me.

04:44.210 --> 04:46.649
Rune, stay behind us.

04:46.650 --> 04:47.210
Okay.

04:47.530 --> 04:50.129
Grant us the power to surpass
our physical limits!

04:50.130 --> 04:51.590
Physical Enchant!

04:51.930 --> 04:53.219
Refresh Mana!

04:53.220 --> 04:55.720
(Enhanced Arm Strength, Enhanced Leg
Strength, Refresh Mana, Enhanced Stamina)

05:08.820 --> 05:10.269
What are those?

05:10.270 --> 05:12.820
Corrupted beings—the Malignant.

05:13.470 --> 05:16.829
Giant termites
that devour worlds, basically.

05:16.830 --> 05:18.080
They're pretty tough.

05:21.660 --> 05:23.719
Clover! Prepare for combat!

05:23.720 --> 05:26.369
Rain, Jamie, start off
with offensive magic!

05:26.370 --> 05:27.289
Right.

05:27.290 --> 05:28.210
Got it.

05:28.540 --> 05:30.789
Forbidden zone locked in ice,

05:30.790 --> 05:32.720
ruled by the snow queen...

05:33.080 --> 05:36.720
Mother Earth, sacred mountain that has
towered over all since ancient times...

05:37.070 --> 05:39.439
Silk, distract them and slow them down!

05:39.440 --> 05:39.919
Right!

05:39.920 --> 05:41.159
Nene, seek and destroy!

05:41.160 --> 05:41.799
Got it!

05:41.800 --> 05:44.189
Marina, watch for the right moment
and charge!

05:44.190 --> 05:45.060
I'm on it!

05:45.450 --> 05:46.400
What about me?

05:47.840 --> 05:51.309
Just kidding. I'll be doing as I please.

05:51.310 --> 05:53.419
I'll leave that thing to you.

05:53.420 --> 05:56.330
You know why, right?
Because only you can handle it.

05:56.580 --> 05:58.799
Violently blow beneath the frozen star!

05:58.800 --> 06:01.330
Grade 5 Magic: Blizzard!

06:03.750 --> 06:06.309
Boulders, fly like a storm!

06:06.310 --> 06:08.750
Grade 5 Magic: Rock Storm!

06:15.550 --> 06:17.010
It's so tough!

06:19.010 --> 06:19.770
Snare!

06:20.530 --> 06:21.229
(Snare)

06:21.230 --> 06:21.889
Finish it!

06:21.890 --> 06:23.020
Right!

06:23.770 --> 06:26.930
I just gotta think of them
as armored warriors!

06:27.400 --> 06:29.470
Magic Blade!

06:30.280 --> 06:31.789
Maybe we can overcome them!

06:31.790 --> 06:32.760
Watch out!

06:34.010 --> 06:34.650
Silk!

06:37.030 --> 06:39.130
Are you all right, Yuke?

06:40.730 --> 06:41.540
Silk?!

06:41.820 --> 06:44.160
Biblion told me...

06:45.250 --> 06:48.040
that the dragon was about to
unleash an invisible attack...

06:51.300 --> 06:55.039
Okay, got it. Thanks, Silk and Biblion.

06:55.040 --> 06:57.300
I'll heal her. Leave this to me.

06:58.000 --> 07:00.829
Gods, grant your healing
to this injured one.

07:00.830 --> 07:01.900
Healing!

07:02.890 --> 07:04.310
Rain, how's she looking?

07:04.810 --> 07:06.230
This... scares me.

07:06.910 --> 07:09.210
It isn't a physical power.

07:09.670 --> 07:12.559
I think... it's conceptual.

07:12.560 --> 07:13.469
Conceptual?

07:13.470 --> 07:15.570
But it's okay. I can heal her.

07:19.690 --> 07:21.200
Now you've done it.

07:23.360 --> 07:25.439
Yuke! I'll hold these off!

07:25.440 --> 07:26.960
You have to stop that thing!

07:29.090 --> 07:29.749
I won't let you!

07:29.750 --> 07:30.340
Rune!

07:32.040 --> 07:32.960
Wish!

07:34.970 --> 07:38.059
Magic? No... the power of wishing?

07:38.060 --> 07:41.010
Leave this to me, Yuke. I'll handle it.

07:41.490 --> 07:43.720
I can be useful to all of you, too!

07:44.080 --> 07:45.919
I appreciate it! Thanks!

07:45.920 --> 07:47.849
I'm all right now, too.

07:47.850 --> 07:49.719
Yuke, leave these to us!

07:49.720 --> 07:51.349
We won't let them get to you!

07:51.350 --> 07:53.610
Go get that thing!

07:54.600 --> 07:58.099
Yuke, it's okay. I'm with you.

07:58.100 --> 07:59.620
Together always.

08:02.160 --> 08:03.040
Wish!

08:04.290 --> 08:06.120
Scent of decaying roses...

08:12.590 --> 08:13.589
Rune!

08:13.590 --> 08:17.220
Sea that swallows the light of the
setting sun as the black dog howls...

08:22.390 --> 08:23.260
Yuke!

08:24.140 --> 08:25.639
Light Shield!

08:25.640 --> 08:29.900
With the mingling of black and white,
souls vanish into chaos!

08:32.800 --> 08:35.009
Well done, Yuke.

08:35.010 --> 08:36.530
We've won this!

08:36.960 --> 08:39.280
I know you can do it. I'll be fine.

08:43.050 --> 08:45.370
Taste this! Grade 5 Magic...

08:49.620 --> 08:53.000
Prismatic Missile!

09:10.320 --> 09:12.600
It's no use. Every part of
you is being contaminated

09:13.160 --> 09:15.550
by the curse—by Prismatic Missile.

09:16.040 --> 09:18.620
The very moment a tainted being is born...

09:20.140 --> 09:20.690
it dies.

09:30.280 --> 09:31.840
The battle is over.

09:32.460 --> 09:34.710
You all did great.

09:39.720 --> 09:45.720
I hope... you've seen... what my
student is capable of, culling.

09:46.130 --> 09:47.340
Uncle Saga!

09:48.490 --> 09:50.340
Don't cry, Yuke.

09:50.750 --> 09:52.850
You don't want to worry your friends.

09:53.360 --> 09:55.860
You're a hero.

09:56.570 --> 09:58.330
You did splendidly.

09:59.130 --> 10:03.360
Sorry, but I'll have to
ask you to finish up.

10:04.470 --> 10:05.370
Okay.

10:22.250 --> 10:25.389
Everyone, this is the Abyss Gate.

10:25.390 --> 10:27.449
It's so pretty.

10:27.450 --> 10:29.729
Your dream came true!

10:29.730 --> 10:31.010
Congratulations!

10:31.660 --> 10:34.519
Thanks. I owe it to all of you.

10:34.520 --> 10:38.140
Is that another world on the other side?

10:38.410 --> 10:41.030
It's one of the other worlds, yes.

10:41.530 --> 10:43.899
There's an infinite number of them.

10:43.900 --> 10:46.849
So this is what you wanted to see, huh?

10:46.850 --> 10:49.999
I think I get it now. Right, Rune?

10:50.000 --> 10:50.789
Yeah.

10:50.790 --> 10:51.409
- Cam!
- Sel!

10:51.410 --> 10:53.790
Clover, mission accomplished.

11:07.530 --> 11:11.130
Okay, time to do that cleanup
my uncle asked me to handle.

11:11.760 --> 11:13.640
I'm going to close the Abyss Gate.

11:16.730 --> 11:19.209
Do you think it's possible?

11:19.210 --> 11:21.150
Yes, I think so.

11:21.500 --> 11:22.899
Thank goodness.

11:22.900 --> 11:25.610
Now the Tenebre throughout
the world should vanish, right?

11:25.980 --> 11:27.610
It should have cleared up already.

11:28.210 --> 11:31.359
That dragon itself was
the culling, after all.

11:31.360 --> 11:34.489
So that means the world
is safe now, right?

11:34.490 --> 11:38.130
Exactly.
Or it will be, once we close this.

11:38.490 --> 11:41.000
And how do we close it?

11:42.170 --> 11:43.759
From the other side.

11:43.760 --> 11:44.909
Yuke!

11:44.910 --> 11:45.749
Yuke...

11:45.750 --> 11:46.949
Yuke?

11:46.950 --> 11:48.260
What does that mean?

11:50.420 --> 11:54.889
I'm going to use my Scroll of Exit to
send all of you back to the surface.

11:54.890 --> 11:56.719
I knew that was what you meant!

11:56.720 --> 11:57.900
Don't do it, Yuke!

11:58.240 --> 12:01.679
Sorry, Jamie. This was already decided.

12:01.680 --> 12:03.150
I'm closing the Abyss Gate.

12:04.020 --> 12:06.009
You mean you're staying behind?

12:06.010 --> 12:09.530
You can't! You're the one who said an
adventure isn't over until you're back home!

12:09.900 --> 12:11.669
You're right, Marina.

12:11.670 --> 12:14.859
But I'm not going home this time.

12:14.860 --> 12:17.290
It's the only way to close the Abyss Gate.

12:17.720 --> 12:22.039
It seems this artifact can only
be closed from the other side.

12:22.040 --> 12:26.189
Um, Yuke... Can't we all go?

12:26.190 --> 12:29.049
Then if we use the Scroll of Exit...

12:29.050 --> 12:30.299
No.

12:30.300 --> 12:32.209
We don't know what kind of world it is,

12:32.210 --> 12:33.769
if we can survive there

12:33.770 --> 12:37.019
or if we'll even be able
to keep our humanity.

12:37.020 --> 12:39.439
We could turn into something
like that dragon.

12:39.440 --> 12:41.940
You're leaving us behind?

12:42.630 --> 12:44.180
It's not that...

12:44.700 --> 12:47.440
No, it is that. I'm sorry.

12:49.200 --> 12:54.579
Th-Then why don't we leave for now,
figure out a plan, and come back?

12:54.580 --> 12:58.789
Marina is right!
There must be another way!

12:58.790 --> 13:01.829
We've defeated the dragon,
so we have time!

13:01.830 --> 13:07.009
Uncle Saga spent over ten years
searching for a way to resolve this,

13:07.010 --> 13:11.160
and despite how much it troubled him,
he concluded that he had to use me.

13:11.680 --> 13:14.079
I've accepted that as well.

13:14.080 --> 13:18.350
There's no guarantee that we'll be able
to stop the culling if it comes again.

13:19.080 --> 13:20.070
Please understand.

13:20.670 --> 13:22.410
I'm going with you!

13:23.300 --> 13:25.309
You can't! I can't take you!

13:25.310 --> 13:29.360
I can't be selfish... and let my
pipe dream of saving the world...

13:30.170 --> 13:31.860
end in me losing you.

13:32.430 --> 13:35.729
You say that, but you look
like you're going to cry!

13:35.730 --> 13:37.789
I won't leave you alone!

13:37.790 --> 13:39.740
This is the life I've chosen!

13:40.350 --> 13:42.219
I feel the same way!

13:42.220 --> 13:44.750
I could go anywhere
as long as I'm with you!

13:45.260 --> 13:47.049
I'll go with you, too!

13:47.050 --> 13:51.000
Even if it means my death,
I can't let you go alone!

13:51.510 --> 13:53.749
I'm going, too, of course!

13:53.750 --> 13:56.260
You're the one who gave me
a place to belong!

13:56.830 --> 13:59.119
You really are an idiot, you know that?

13:59.120 --> 14:02.010
If you're gonna seduce someone,
at least see it through.

14:02.710 --> 14:06.270
Thanks, all of you. I'm so blessed.

14:07.040 --> 14:08.879
And that's why I can't take you.

14:08.880 --> 14:13.530
You guys are the most
important things in this world.

14:14.100 --> 14:16.400
Check! Scroll of Exit!

14:17.780 --> 14:18.650
Yuke!

14:19.150 --> 14:20.199
Yuke!

14:20.200 --> 14:21.040
Don't do this!

14:21.890 --> 14:22.960
Wish.

14:29.080 --> 14:31.049
Clover disappeared!

14:31.050 --> 14:31.849
What happened?

14:31.850 --> 14:32.920
Where'd they go?

14:34.160 --> 14:37.290
Did you guys all make it out?

14:38.440 --> 14:39.559
Rune!

14:39.560 --> 14:40.603
- It's Clover!
- They're alive!

14:40.604 --> 14:41.769
Why are they here?!

14:41.770 --> 14:44.139
Someone let the Adventurer's Guild know!

14:44.140 --> 14:50.899
I wished that all of you could
get back to Finis safely.

14:50.900 --> 14:52.519
That's okay, right?

14:52.520 --> 14:55.530
It's what I wanted from
the bottom of my heart.

14:56.160 --> 14:58.030
How is this okay, Rune?!

14:58.290 --> 15:01.149
No... Rune, that's not the answer!

15:01.150 --> 15:03.270
It's me! This is my job!

15:03.890 --> 15:06.540
We made this decision
before entering Tenebre!

15:06.830 --> 15:10.179
Yeah. I was supposed to be last,

15:10.180 --> 15:13.050
but I jumped the line. Sorry.

15:13.490 --> 15:16.430
I just love all of you so much!

15:16.770 --> 15:18.679
You can't do this, Rune! Stop!

15:18.680 --> 15:22.060
I promised I'd make you happy!

15:22.410 --> 15:27.129
I know, but this is what makes me happy.

15:27.130 --> 15:31.029
For all of you to be happy forever,

15:31.030 --> 15:34.570
to never be apart. That's my wish.

15:34.890 --> 15:38.729
Rune, wait! We'll head
back in there right now!

15:38.730 --> 15:41.830
Don't you dare do this!
I'll be lecturing you later!

15:42.660 --> 15:46.119
Thank you, Marina and Silk.

15:46.120 --> 15:48.229
But this is for the best.

15:48.230 --> 15:50.839
If I stay here, the roots
of the culling will remain.

15:50.840 --> 15:54.139
Yuke will take care of that!

15:54.140 --> 15:56.249
Thank you, too, Nene.

15:56.250 --> 15:58.590
I had lots of fun in the bath with you!

15:59.020 --> 16:02.459
You haven't even been to
an amusement park yet!

16:02.460 --> 16:06.600
You promised you'd go with me,
the guild master, and Mamar someday!

16:06.960 --> 16:11.479
Yeah. I really wanted to go
to an amusement park with you.

16:11.480 --> 16:13.360
I wonder what they're like.

16:13.820 --> 16:15.740
Exactly! So you...

16:16.490 --> 16:18.989
You should stay with us longer!

16:18.990 --> 16:21.239
It's okay, Rain.

16:21.240 --> 16:24.490
I've had plenty of fun with you already.

16:25.050 --> 16:28.979
Oh, but if I can be reborn,
I'd like to be an author.

16:28.980 --> 16:32.250
I'll go on lots of adventures
and write lots of stories!

16:32.650 --> 16:35.189
I'll bring excitement to so many people!

16:35.190 --> 16:38.920
And when my book is published,
I might even get to autograph it...

16:39.440 --> 16:40.890
Doesn't that sound wonderful?

16:41.930 --> 16:44.260
Yeah. It's a great idea.

16:45.090 --> 16:45.940
Right?

16:46.990 --> 16:49.270
Well, I'm going now.

16:51.870 --> 16:52.770
Rune!

16:53.870 --> 16:58.809
Yuke, everyone, thank you so much!
I mean it!

16:58.810 --> 17:01.030
I was so happy with you!

17:07.470 --> 17:08.469
Rune...

17:08.470 --> 17:09.249
Cam...

17:09.250 --> 17:09.930
Sel...

17:13.510 --> 17:16.419
Rune... No!

17:16.420 --> 17:18.669
This isn't right!

17:18.670 --> 17:21.919
How in the world could she just...

17:21.920 --> 17:24.230
Why, Rune?

17:30.520 --> 17:31.639
It's wrong.

17:31.640 --> 17:35.309
Yeah. This is wrong, isn't it?

17:35.310 --> 17:37.799
Yuke, let's think positive.

17:37.800 --> 17:38.440
Rain...

17:38.770 --> 17:41.449
Rune didn't cry. She was smiling.

17:41.450 --> 17:44.209
She saved us, after all.

17:44.210 --> 17:46.379
By her own free will and resolve.

17:46.380 --> 17:49.229
So we have to respect that.

17:49.230 --> 17:52.890
We have to make her wish,
her desire, come true.

17:53.610 --> 17:55.580
Yeah. You're right.

18:01.310 --> 18:02.040
Rune...

18:08.840 --> 18:09.370
Come in.

18:10.480 --> 18:14.250
Pardon the intrusion, Yuke. I brought tea.

18:14.770 --> 18:16.420
Thanks, Silk.

18:17.960 --> 18:20.270
What are you writing?

18:20.690 --> 18:22.919
Sort of a journal, I guess.

18:22.920 --> 18:27.049
This month has been pretty...
well, I think "turbulent" sums it up.

18:27.050 --> 18:29.619
I wanted to get my memories of it
in order.

18:29.620 --> 18:32.869
You're right. It was definitely turbulent.

18:32.870 --> 18:34.770
After we got back
from Achromatic Darkness...

18:36.450 --> 18:39.639
People called us the heroes
who saved the world,

18:39.640 --> 18:44.589
gave us medals, and called us to all
kinds of weird meetings and assemblies.

18:44.590 --> 18:46.969
I'm clueless when it
comes to noble etiquette,

18:46.970 --> 18:49.059
so I thought it was gonna give me ulcers.

18:49.060 --> 18:50.219
Same goes for me.

18:50.220 --> 18:53.930
But I was able to properly
send off my uncle,

18:54.560 --> 18:57.179
and we got to see Mastoma again.
That made me happy.

18:57.180 --> 19:02.549
King Vincent even invited the
prince here as an honored guest.

19:02.550 --> 19:07.189
His contributions through all this won
him a good chance at being the next king.

19:07.190 --> 19:09.769
I'm glad I was able to
be of some use to him.

19:09.770 --> 19:11.789
More than just "some"!

19:11.790 --> 19:14.779
You saved Salmutaria, Yuke!

19:14.780 --> 19:16.759
It wasn't just me.

19:16.760 --> 19:18.289
All of Clover did that.

19:18.290 --> 19:20.119
Thank you for saying so,

19:20.120 --> 19:25.040
but I never thought I'd be
named a dungeon count like you.

19:25.370 --> 19:27.179
Your talents were rewarded,

19:27.180 --> 19:32.649
A-rank adventurer and fellow
dungeon count, Silk Amberwood.

19:32.650 --> 19:35.969
And thanks to that, I get
to go see your homeland.

19:35.970 --> 19:37.180
This is work, you know.

19:37.620 --> 19:39.969
Yeah, but we can't just decide on our own

19:39.970 --> 19:43.069
to make a princess from another
country a noble of Welmelia.

19:43.070 --> 19:46.820
The king was looking out for us when
he sent us on this courtesy call.

19:47.170 --> 19:49.479
Sounds like a plausible
excuse for a vacation.

19:49.480 --> 19:50.190
True!

19:50.730 --> 19:55.849
Still, I really hope your grandfather
isn't going to kill me.

19:55.850 --> 19:59.829
What if he says I'm a criminal who
kidnapped a dark elf princess?

19:59.830 --> 20:01.099
That is possible...

20:01.100 --> 20:01.960
It is?!

20:04.440 --> 20:06.960
Biblion says no such future exists.

20:08.400 --> 20:11.949
That said, I'm a bit nervous, as well.

20:11.950 --> 20:17.099
I fled my homeland before.
How should I act there now?

20:17.100 --> 20:20.390
I get it. But it'll work out.

20:21.000 --> 20:23.909
You're right. I'll be going, then.

20:23.910 --> 20:26.100
Thanks for the tea, Princess.

20:26.680 --> 20:28.620
No teasing!

20:33.950 --> 20:34.860
Good stuff.

20:50.220 --> 20:52.320
We really have been through a lot.

20:52.790 --> 20:54.130
Yuke.

20:54.510 --> 20:56.219
Rain, what's up?

20:56.220 --> 20:57.369
This.

20:57.370 --> 20:59.949
Oh, we didn't return it to Mastoma!

20:59.950 --> 21:02.300
Not that. Look closer.

21:05.130 --> 21:06.139
What is it?

21:06.140 --> 21:07.850
It's pointing at Rune.

21:08.890 --> 21:11.740
She must be in some other world.

21:12.260 --> 21:13.239
Yeah!

21:13.240 --> 21:15.319
You think she was reborn?

21:15.320 --> 21:16.490
Maybe!

21:16.980 --> 21:19.240
You think she became an author?

21:19.600 --> 21:21.869
Hard to say.

21:21.870 --> 21:24.740
But I'm sure she's happy.

21:25.390 --> 21:29.050
She's the Golden Priestess who's
received all of our blessings.

21:29.740 --> 21:30.630
Yeah.

21:31.680 --> 21:35.619
Well... Rune told us to be happy,

21:35.620 --> 21:37.459
but how do I make that happen?

21:37.460 --> 21:38.870
That's easy.

21:45.970 --> 21:47.920
See? We're happy!

21:49.770 --> 21:52.849
Hey! Yuke's hugging Rain!

21:52.850 --> 21:53.669
No fair!

21:53.670 --> 21:55.879
No getting the jump on us! You're guilty!

21:55.880 --> 21:58.029
I demand Nene time!

21:58.030 --> 21:59.619
This again?

21:59.620 --> 22:01.879
You cause a big fuss like this every time.

22:01.880 --> 22:03.789
You should think things through more.

22:03.790 --> 22:06.659
You can't blame him.
Yuke is Yuke, after all.

22:06.660 --> 22:08.040
- Cam!
- Sel!

22:09.110 --> 22:10.970
I am number one, though.

22:13.010 --> 22:17.319
Well, we'll reach Silk's
homeland, Vilmullen, tomorrow.

22:17.320 --> 22:19.139
Is everyone ready?

22:19.140 --> 22:20.140
I am!

22:20.500 --> 22:21.530
All set!

22:22.110 --> 22:23.469
I'm... not.

22:23.470 --> 22:25.779
I'll help you out later.

22:25.780 --> 22:28.099
Thanks, Jamie! I love you!

22:28.100 --> 22:31.399
Jamie, please try not to spoil Marina.

22:31.400 --> 22:34.059
Aw, what's it gonna hurt?

22:34.060 --> 22:35.220
No means no.

22:36.040 --> 22:39.369
It'll be our first time there.
No telling what'll happen,

22:39.370 --> 22:41.359
but we'll be fine since we're together.

22:41.360 --> 22:42.769
Because we're Clover!

22:42.770 --> 22:43.240
Cam!

22:43.570 --> 22:44.450
Right!

22:44.740 --> 22:45.619
Yeah.

22:45.620 --> 22:46.699
- Sel!
- Okay!

22:46.700 --> 22:48.159
Let's do this!

22:48.160 --> 22:49.660
Without a doubt.

22:50.120 --> 22:53.000
Okay! Let's have fun, but be careful!

22:56.420 --> 22:57.639
Thank you...

22:57.640 --> 22:59.529
...for watching!

22:59.530 --> 23:00.570
Cam!
